From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: KDA state rows carry the pad's common width again

The pin sizes every KDA input row with cuda_kda_block.rowWidth, which returns
the one padded width all ranks share when TF_GLM_KDA_PAD is on (8,728 columns
at TP=3, from the widest rank's 22 heads). Patch 0003 replaced those four
sizings in cuda_state.zig with paddedWidth(own raw width), an older form: on a
rank holding 21 heads that is 8,344 columns, while the projection, the chain
and the conv window (matWidth) still read and write 8,728 columns a row. With
the pad on, ranks 1 and 2 therefore ran 384 columns past their rows.

Seen in the serve as replies that depend on batching: with the pad on, the
same prompt returned one digest at one stream but four at two streams and
eight at four and six (three rounds of the same prompts), where a stable
engine returns one digest a prompt. This restores the pin's four lines and
removes paddedWidth, which nothing else read.

Patch 0024 also left tileLinears calling padKdaInputs twice. padOneKdaInput
compares against the unpadded width, so the second call copied each padded
stack into a second buffer; one call remains.

With the pad off both forms give the raw width, so the default path is
unchanged.

Receipt (spark1-3, TP=3, drafts on, TF_GLM_KDA_PAD=1 and no other knob,
streams.py prose, 400 tokens, 3 rounds, a fresh boot a level; before is the
stack through 0039, after is through 0041): before, the 1 / 2 / 4 / 4 prompts
of 1 / 2 / 4 / 6 streams returned 1 / 4 / 8 / 8 distinct digests; after, 1 / 2
/ 4 / 4 / 4 at 1 / 2 / 4 / 6 / 8 streams. Decode with the pad, tok/s at 1 / 2 /
4 / 6 / 8: 56.59 / 69.77 / 87.83 / 119.63 / 132.46 before, 63.94 / 74.66 /
93.28 / 124.59 / 150.80 after; tokens a round at one stream 2.24 before, 2.75
after. With the pad off the after image returns the pin's digests at every
level.

diff --git a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_kda_block.zig b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_kda_block.zig
--- a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_kda_block.zig
+++ b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_kda_block.zig
@@ -48,13 +48,6 @@
 
 /// TF_GLM_KDA_PAD's one eight-aligned row width for every rank, set once at load (Engine.open); 0: no pad.
 pub var pad_to: usize = 0;
-pub fn paddedWidth(raw: usize) usize {
-    if (raw % 8 == 0) return raw;
-    const v = std.c.getenv("TF_GLM_KDA_PAD") orelse return raw;
-    const t = std.mem.trim(u8, std.mem.span(v), " ");
-    if (t.len == 0 or std.mem.eql(u8, t, "0")) return raw;
-    return std.mem.alignForward(usize, raw, 8);
-}
 
 /// TF_GLM_KDA_DUMP: driver and path for one dump of a projection's output, set at load, spent on first use.
 pub var dump_driver: ?*const cuda.Driver = null;
diff --git a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_state.zig b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_state.zig
--- a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_state.zig
+++ b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_state.zig
